{
  "criteriaSatisfied": [
    {
      "id": "criterion-1",
      "status": "satisfied",
      "evidence": "Wrote detailed findings to context.md covering 6 frames with specific bugs: rendering instability in Scene3D (frames 003/005 showing blank/degenerate scenes), strike-zone box mispositioning (frame_007/009), missing ball mesh during animation, and persistent watermark overlay colliding with stat UI in every frame - all with severity ratings and inferred source file locations (src/components/Scene3D.tsx, src/components/PitchHero.tsx)"
    }
  ],
  "changedFiles": [
    ".pi-subagents/artifacts/outputs/5edc4595/context.md"
  ],
  "testsAddedOrUpdated": [],
  "commandsRun": [
    {
      "command": "ls -la /tmp/video-frames/",
      "result": "passed",
      "summary": "confirmed 11 frame files exist, read frames 001,003,005,007,009,011"
    }
  ],
  "validationOutput": [
    "context.md written successfully (7456 bytes) to authoritative output path"
  ],
  "residualRisks": [
    "Analysis is based solely on visual inspection of screenshots; without access to actual source code line numbers, root-cause attribution to Scene3D.tsx/PitchHero.tsx is inferred from project docs, not confirmed by code read",
    "Watermark overlay could be an external screen-recording tool artifact rather than an in-app bug - flagged as low-confidence/needs verification",
    "Only 6 of 11 available frames were analyzed per task instructions; frames 002,004,006,008,010 were not reviewed and could contain additional detail on the transition moments"
  ],
  "noStagedFiles": true,
  "diffSummary": "Created new markdown context file summarizing visual bug analysis of 6 video frames from MLB Pitch Visualizer, no source code changed",
  "reviewFindings": [
    "high: Scene3D rendering appears unstable/incomplete during pitch animation frames (003, 005) - blank or near-empty 3D scene rendered, likely camera or mesh mount/unmount issue in src/components/Scene3D.tsx",
    "medium: Strike zone box position inconsistent across frames (007, 009 show it disconnected from home plate) versus correct position in idle/result frames (001, 011)",
    "medium: No visible baseball sphere mesh during 'Pitching...' animation state in captured frames; only a shadow/mark dot visible on ground",
    "low: persistent watermark text 'pitches.just-dev.us' overlaps and obscures velocity/spin-rate stat text in all 6 frames - verify if this is in-app or external recording tool overlay"
  ],
  "manualNotes": "Screenshots are from a mobile screen recording (status bar shows red REC pill toggling with clock). The captured frames appear to interleave two separate pitch attempts (idle->pitching->result cycle repeats), so frame ordering may not represent a single continuous animation. Recommend the next agent open Scene3D.tsx and PitchHero.tsx to trace animation state transitions and confirm whether meshes are being remounted mid-animation, which is the most likely cause of the blank-frame rendering bug."
}
```

